Fetch a single track as the artist's own release before a compilation.

Why: a track request picks the release to fetch by the shared MusicBrainz
rank, where the primary type (Album > EP > Single) comes before the
compilation penalty, so a various-artists compilation album beats the
artist's own single. On 2026-10-24 a request for Zombie Nation's "Kernkraft
400" (recording bf2754e5, on the 2006 single "Kernkraft 400 Single Mixes"
and on the 45-track "Wire 08 Compilation") targeted the compilation. Usenet
had the artist's single; DroppedNeedle downloaded it, but held all 14 files
as weak matches ("the album title or artist does not agree with the
release"), and they could not be imported as they were because none of the
single's mixes is on the compilation. A download is named after the
artist's album or single, never after a compilation that lists the track.
The track target now ranks compilations after the artist's own releases,
with Official and version-keeping still deciding first (an official
compilation still beats a bootleg single). The shared rank is unchanged.

Tests: the ordering test pinned "comp before single"; it now pins the
single first. New test for single vs compilation and bootleg single vs
compilation. Both fail without the change. Acquire suites (integration and
lib units, symlink-free TMPDIR): same 2 failures with and without the patch.

Remove when: upstream ranks compilations after the artist's own releases.

